Apply the virtual Linus Torvalds code-quality lens: dead code, logic holes, incomplete conversions (every metric read through hnswMetric or spfreshMetric; every SPFresh entry point through readSPFreshConfig; every former caller of the replaced functions), tests that cannot fail (the samples pin, the queue pin and the entry-point table against the mutation and red evidence), claims wider than the code (comments, DIVERGENCES, CHANGELOG, TODO, 7.19 including its corrected evidence paragraph), and evidence that does not show what it is cited for.
